    "registration": {
      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "LIANG T'ung-shu 梁同書 (T. 元頴, H. 山舟, 不翁, 新吾長翁), Oct. 26, 1723–1815, Aug. 19, scholar and calligrapher, was a native of Ch'ien-t'ang (Hangchow). He was the elder son of Liang Shih-chêng [q. v.] but was adopted by his uncle, Liang Ch'i-hsin 梁啟心 (T. 首存, H. 蔎林, 1695–1758, a chin-shih of 1739).",
          "source": "eccp-3643705",
          "kind": "source-wording",
          "status": "imported"
        },
        {
